{
  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 (config_009, acc=0.520) is our strongest baseline, while image-only with imagenet_vit_l (config_004, acc=0.227) is weak. We have zero multimodal results, so the central open question is whether fusing image features with the best RNA encoder actually improves over RNA alone. Question tested: config_039 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion, no aggregation) is the simplest possible multimodal extension of our best RNA baseline. It isolates the fusion benefit by (a) using the already-validated best RNA encoder, (b) using the image encoder whose standalone performance we already know, (c) keeping singleprofile to match the RNA baseline, and (d) using weighted fusion rather than concat, which can learn to downweight a weak image modality if it does not contribute. Why best next experiment: Under a tight budget, the highest-value question is whether multimodality helps at all before investing in multiprofile, transformer aggregation, or alternative encoders. This experiment gives a clean, interpretable signal: if it beats 0.520, multimodal fusion is worth further exploration; if it does not, we can redirect budget toward RNA encoder or profile-setting improvements. It changes only one design axis (adding image + fusion) relative to config_009, making the result easy to attribute."
}

